</code></pre>

Method Returns Description <code>calculatePositionSize(symbol, riskPercent, stopLossPips)</code> <code>double</code> Lot size risking <code>riskPercent</code>% of balance <code>getMaxLotSize(symbol)</code> <code>double</code> Largest lot the free margin can open <code>canOpenPosition(symbol, volume, reason&amp;)</code> <code>bool</code> Can a <code>volume</code>-lot order open now? <code>reason</code> explains a false <code>calculateRequiredMargin(symbol, volume)</code> <code>double</code> Margin to open <code>volume</code> lots (buy side) <code>calculateSLTP(symbol, direction, entryPrice, slPips, tpPips, slOut&amp;, tpOut&amp;)</code> <code>void</code> Absolute SL/TP prices from pip distances (<code>direction</code> = "buy"/"sell") <pre><code>// Risk 1% of balance on a 20-pip stop, then open that size with SL/TP
double lots = sugar.calculatePositionSize("EURUSD", 1.0, 20);
std::string why;
